Compile flightaware for rpi4b, rpi5, opi5, rockpi4b and rk3328:

Parts required:
1. Car/Indoor Antenna for FlightAware.
2. Band-Pass SMA Filter.
3. ADS-B 1090MHz PRO USB Stick.

cd ~/build-5sbc/flightaware
make clean
make rootfs_base
make CHIP=rk3328 finalize
CHIP=rk3328 ./mk-espimage.sh 
./mk-image.sh

Plugin usb3 stick to PC.  ( rockpi4b use NVMe SSD )
sudo ./mksdcardimg.sh
sudo mount /dev/sda2 /mnt
cp ./flightaware/* /mnt/home/linaro
sync; sudo umount /mnt;
Eject usb3 stick from PC.

Plugin usb3 stick to sbc.  ( rockpi4b use NVMe SSD )
Plugin ethernet cable to opi5 and rk3328.
(rpi4b) Esc -> Device Manager -> Rpi -> Advanced -> 3GB ( disable ) -> F10 -> Boot Manager -> first UEFI or SDCARD.
Login:
Username: linaro
Password: linaro
Setup wifi. Disable power saving, auto suspend and screen saver.
sudo apt update
sudo apt install net-tools openssh-server pulseaudio-utils
sudo ifconfig
ssh-keygen -R 192.168.86.28
ssh linaro@192.168.86.28
df .
sudo resize2fs /dev/sda2 ( for NVMe SSD /dev/nvme0n1p2 )
df .
uname -a
lsb_release -a
sudo dpkg-reconfigure tzdata
sudo dpkg-reconfigure locales
date
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade
sync
free

sudo apt install chrpath tcl-dev python3-dev python3-venv python3-setuptools python3-pip python3-pyelftools libboost-system-dev libboost-program-options-dev libboost-regex-dev libboost-filesystem-dev patchelf itcl3 tcllib tclx8.4 librtlsdr-dev libbladerf-dev libhackrf-dev liblimesuite-dev libsoapysdr-dev libusb-1.0-0-dev pkg-config libncurses5-dev lighttpd tcl-tls netcat-openbsd

See https://www.flightaware.com/adsb/piaware/install
wget https://www.flightaware.com/adsb/piaware/files/packages/pool/piaware/f/flightaware-apt-repository/flightaware-apt-repository_1.3_all.deb
sudo dpkg -i flightaware-apt-repository_1.3_all.deb
sudo apt update
sudo apt install piaware dump1090-fa dump978-fa

Change feeder-id on the last line of piaware.conf or comment out for the first time.
For the first time you need to claim feeder-id from https://www.flightaware.com/adsb/piaware/build after plugin ADS-B 1090MHz PRO USB Stick, filter and antenna.

If you want to use old feeder-id without claiming a new one, change the last line of piaware.conf to use your old feeder-id.

sudo cp piaware.conf /etc
sync
sudo reboot
Connect Antenna to SMA Filter. Connect SMA Filter to ADS-B USB Stick. Plugin ADS-B USB Stick to sbc.
ssh-keygen -R 192.168.86.28
ssh linaro@192.168.86.28
date

./startpiaware
sudo piaware-status  ( run sudo piaware-status serveral times till dump1090 and piaware are connected )

When everything is ok and ready to capture data that you sent to flightaware:

nc 127.0.0.1 30003 | egrep --line-buffered 'MSG,1,|MSG,3,|MSG,5,' >> flight_tracks.csv

After a few minutes, CTRL-C to stop caturing.
vi flight_tracks.csv
It has aircraft's info, date, time, GPS position etc.

./flightdata.py

The website is in https://www.flightaware.com/adsb/stats/user/yourusername
The map is in browser http://192.168.86.234:8080/
